diff --git a/EPHEMERAL_SERVER_PATCH.md b/EPHEMERAL_SERVER_PATCH.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..1de3849e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/EPHEMERAL_SERVER_PATCH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# Experimental ephemeral-content capability
+
+Base: Canvas `ver/26.2`, commit `a631d9d7f16e2ea127cb731a31775206877038be`
+(the source revision of `26.2 build 994-stable`). Java 25 is required.
+This is a local server patch, not an upstream release. Polar's Canvas backend requires it.
+
+## Contract
+
+A Bukkit `ChunkGenerator` implementing `io.canvasmc.canvas.world.EphemeralWorldGenerator`
+opts its world into non-persistent content. The server snapshots this at construction;
+there is no mutable configuration flag. Use an exclusively owned, fresh instance directory.
+Marked worlds start with vanilla autosaving/unloading disabled (`noSave=true`) for RAM retention.
+This does not add ticking tickets or provide void generation, force-unload chunks, change regional
+ownership, or guarantee garbage collection. The immutable content IO guards are independent of `noSave`.
+
+The capability disables reads and writes of chunks (including protochunks), entities, POI
+and per-world saved data. It covers native unloads, autosaves and regional/server shutdown.
+Normal worlds retain their existing persistence behavior. Ancillary administrative files,
+player storage and external-plugin storage are outside the contract.
+
+The guards exist both before serialization and at controller/storage boundaries. Pending
+Moonrise IO operations still complete normally; simply dropping queued operations would
+strand unload tasks. The low-level guards also protect direct storage/scanner paths.
+Existing files are not imported, overwritten or deleted by ephemeral content operations.
+
+Custom NMS creators must use `PaperWorldLoader.loadWorldData(..., true)` and
+`SavedDataStorage(..., true)` before constructing a marked `ServerLevel`. The constructor
+rejects incompatible saved-data storage. Ordinary Bukkit `WorldCreator` handles this itself.
+
+For marked worlds, native halt timeouts and cache-close failures are fatal unload failures,
+not warnings followed by success. Async unload reports `FAIL_RESOURCE_CLOSE` at most once,
+keeps the world in its unloading state and retains Canvas's server-stop safety behavior.
+Do not retry a partially failed native unload or delete its directory. A successful callback
+is not a promise that other plugins or the JVM have released their references.
+
+## Build and tests
+
+`EphemeralChunkLifecycle.contractVersion()` returns 1. `destroyChunk(ServerLevel, x, z)` returns
+a future containing `DESTROYED`, `ALREADY_ABSENT`, `BLOCKED` or `WORLD_DESTROYING`; technical errors
+are exceptional. It dispatches through an existing-region ticketless queue, preserving native
+split/merge routing and retiring tasks when regions disappear. It never loads a missing region,
+adds a scheduler ticket, removes foreign tickets or forcibly removes non-unloadable entities.
+Destruction uses the native holder's three unload stages and existing ticket/scheduling locks.
+
+```sh
+./gradlew applyAllPatches
+./gradlew :canvas-server:test --tests io.canvasmc.canvas.world.EphemeralStorageTestSuite
+./gradlew createPaperclipJar :canvas-server:ephemeralIntegrationTestPlugin
+```
+
+Server: `canvas-server/build/libs/canvas-paperclip-26.2.local-SNAPSHOT.jar`.
+The opt-in test plugin is `canvas-server/build/libs/EphemeralStorageIntegration.jar`.
+**Never put this test plugin on a production server:** it creates worlds and stops the server.
+Use an empty disposable directory, accept the Minecraft EULA yourself, and launch with Java 25.
+The plugin writes `ephemeral-capability-result.txt`; `PASS assertions=14` is the expected result.
+
+Validated locally:
+
+- Ten unit tests: all three controllers, direct existing/absent region storage, saved data,
+  native pre-serialization guards, generation/IO halt failures, aggregate cache-close failures,
+  exactly-once unload completion after failure, and ticketless queue execution/retirement without IO or tickets.
+- Actual patched Canvas boot: generated a chunk with a block entity, entity and POI; invoked
+  the native shutdown-save path; unloaded using `save=false`; observed no content files.
+  A normal world still wrote block/entity/POI regions and unloaded successfully (14 assertions).
+
+The separate Polar repository supplies a two-regional-thread lifecycle integration plugin/runner.
+Its actual patched-server run passed 28 assertions: targeted destruction across distant regions,
+ticket blockers, absent chunks, void revisit, checked/cancelled unload, cleanup retry, and weak-reference
+collection of chunks while the world remains loaded followed by collection of the detached world.
+Not yet validated exhaustively: split/merge stress, players and teleport races, sustained memory plateau,
+heap analysis, crash/restart, and injected real-server shutdown failures. The storage-only smoke test
+used one regional tick thread. No production-readiness claim is made. Human review is required
+before upstream submission.
